- the lone **green‑shirted player standing by himself on the far left**, right up against the touchline — he's the nearest player of all;
- the **referee/official in dark blue** standing just behind the pack;
- the **scrum itself** (the red‑and‑blue and green forwards bound together mid‑picture) together with the **green player standing at its right edge**, since the scrum has been formed fairly close to that side of the pitch.

The players farther down the frame — the green **No. 21** waiting in the foreground and the green player on the right‑hand side — are many metres out into the field of play and would be well clear of the falling stand.
